1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:07,660
Good flats go in days. Inky just sent
me the three best that fit my plan.

2
00:00:08,200 --> 00:00:10,048
I described it once:

3
00:00:10,088 --> 00:00:16,468
€200,000, a flat to rent out, prices
rising, easy for a Dutch buyer.

4
00:00:16,508 --> 00:00:21,660
Inky asked what it couldn't guess, then
wrote the plan.

5
00:00:22,200 --> 00:00:28,801
Through Apify it read nearly 18,000 real
listings in Porto, Bari and Łódź.

6
00:00:28,841 --> 00:00:33,468
An open model wrote rules, and the data
tested them:

7
00:00:33,508 --> 00:00:39,660
15, 70, then 46 homes. Porto's prices
climb, but the rents don't pay.

8
00:00:40,200 --> 00:00:45,327
Tecnocasa, Italy's largest agency network,
had no Apify scraper.

9
00:00:45,367 --> 00:00:51,301
Inky used it once, found its data feed,
and published its own Apify actor.

10
00:00:51,341 --> 00:00:55,660
Eight windows, no model: 96 flats in under
20 seconds.

11
00:00:56,200 --> 00:01:00,632
Inky built this n8n workflow itself,
through the API.

12
00:01:00,672 --> 00:01:07,298
Every 15 minutes, five Apify scrapers feed
compiled scoring. No AI. Last night:

13
00:01:07,338 --> 00:01:09,660
36 runs, 9,009 listings.

14
00:01:10,200 --> 00:01:12,903
I broke one step on purpose.

15
00:01:12,943 --> 00:01:14,961
n8n caught the error.

16
00:01:15,001 --> 00:01:22,994
The open model read it and fixed the input
in 7 seconds, then published it and ran it again.

17
00:01:23,034 --> 00:01:24,660
It told me after.

18
00:01:25,200 --> 00:01:27,713
I type one line:

19
00:01:27,753 --> 00:01:32,089
"only places with the euro." 46 homes
become 14.

20
00:01:32,129 --> 00:01:34,460
On Telegram I approve one;

21
00:01:34,500 --> 00:01:40,660
the email to the agent waits in Gmail, as
a draft. Inky never sends.

22
00:01:41,200 --> 00:01:43,660
Share it in a sentence.

23
00:01:44,200 --> 00:01:51,660
Inky. Tell it once. It watches every 15
minutes; you only decide.

